WEBVTT

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.260
<i>Cruel Blade!</i>

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:57.410
Hey.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.620
Who are you?

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.360
<i>Thinking back,</i>

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.910
<i>this is where everything 
began going wrong.</i>

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.020
<i>Probably.</i>

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:49.390
<i>Ever since I was little, 
trouble has always had a way of finding me.</i>

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.220
I can't breathe...

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.790
The doors on the right side will open.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.000
Please be careful.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:55.900
Finally there...

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.350
What is this?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.200
I'm getting off! I'm getting off!

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.000
No!

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.500
I'll be late again!

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:21.330
Oda Nobunaga was born in 1534.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.810
He is, without doubt, the most famous

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.810
general of the Warring States era.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:31.970
Begining with his unification 
of Owari, in 1559,

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:35.020
continuing with his Okehazama battle 
with Imagawa Yoshimoto...

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.020
Hideyoshi.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.440
Here.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.360
Tokunyan.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.200
Thanks.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.680
Quietly, quietly...

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.250
Hide-san?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.410
You're late again?

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:15.340
<i>But I never expected that to happen!</i>

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:22.070
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:22.070
<b>A Maiden Teleported</b>

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.950
Why are you always late?

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.290
I can't get off the train.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.100
It gets so crowded during rush hour...

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.830
Don't touch that!

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.730
You're so mean, Date-sensei!

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.370
I'm not.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.440
Anyway, you can just take an earlier train.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.520
You're right, but I can't get up any earlier.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.580
I'm at my limit now!

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.740
You should just go to bed earlier.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.740
You're right, but...

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.250
I've got things to do at night.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.520
Things?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.480
Looking at my favorite idol, 
Tama-chan's blog,

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.630
checking out the net auctions, 
reading magazines,

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:01.370
and texting my friends!

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.170
And then, there are late night snacks...

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:06.850
So next thing I know, 
it's already really late.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:08.910
Hide-san.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.910
It's good to have lots of interests,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.670
but try to study a little and not just play.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.830
I'm not playing!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.130
Sorry, but fashion and snacks are my life.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.360
I'm not playing!

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.410
Right, right.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:25.500
I understand.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.760
Do you really, Date-sensei?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.710
Listen, if you fail the next test,

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:35.270
you'll have make-up classes 
all the way until summer vacation.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.730
Seriously?

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:38.900
Seriously.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.300
Now... Go home and study.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.180
I've got something to do today,

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.010
so I don't have much time.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.490
That's so cold of you.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.290
Your student is having 
a really hard time.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.520
First, do your best.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.250
If that's not enough, I might help you out.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.910
Akerin, what should I do?

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.380
What should you do?

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.640
You should study for your test.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:11.350
You should at least remember 
Toyotomi Hideyoshi.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.300
You're nicknamed "Hideyoshi," after all.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.930
I just can't, Tokunyan.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.140
I didn't get it

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.340
because I liked that 
Toyotomi Hidekichi guy, anyway.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.730
Hidekichi...

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:24.870
I guess calling you Hideyoshi 
because your name's

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.860
Hideyoshino is pretty straightforward.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.100
Anyway, you'll be in big trouble

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.240
if you don't seriously start studying.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:35.540
My free and lovely after-school time...

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.740
What should I do?

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.980
I prayed to God, and I got a BR Riichi!

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:43.510
God answered my prayers!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.020
Praying to a god...

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:53.260
<b>Pass Your Tests</b>

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:53.260
Will my wish come true?

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.930
These stairs just go on and on.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.820
And they're so steep.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.270
And this place feels really scary...

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.780
And it's dark.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.400
It's like a horror movie!

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.280
I'm here, but...

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.790
See, no one's here.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.580
Omikuji fortunes?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.210
Well, I like testing my luck 
more than relying on a god.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.720
This is perfect!

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.680
Oh, the money, right!

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.020
OK! Perfect!

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:44.090
Now I won't need any make-up classes!

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.550
I haven't prayed yet!

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.530
What should I do?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.050
I only have 1 yen left, for the whole month...

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.420
Is that too little, maybe?

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.330
I only have this much right now,

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.140
but I'll pay the rest, once I get promoted.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.960
Did I do that right?

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.920
No! My after-school life!

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:16.800
What's that?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.130
Someone's there.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.480
What is this?

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:28.290
Wow...

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.320
What?

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.450
Oh, no!

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:26.790
Huh?

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.650
I fell asleep.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:36.430
Am I in a park? No... A forest?

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.300
How?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.650
A mountain?

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.010
What's that?

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:44.690
A campfire?

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.430
That's not a campfire!

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.280
A fire!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.800
Fire department!

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.200
I've gotta call 119!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.010
Someone's there!

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.820
Excuse me!

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:06.870
Are you OK?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.040
We need to call the fire department...

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.290
Akerin!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.910
I'm so relieved...

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.680
Akerin, I went to this temple,

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.410
and all this weird stuff happened.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.780
What's going on here?

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:18.910
There's a fire!

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.350
Did you call the fire department?

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.260
Akerin?

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.080
What are you talking about?

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.420
I don't know you!

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:26.750
Hey!

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:29.850
That's not funny at all right now!

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.780
Villains!

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.840
Who are these people?

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.050
Arsonists?

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:43.320
Robbers?

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.420
Hey!

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.000
We'll talk later!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.320
Were you the ones who 
attacked this village?!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.190
<i>Cruel Blade!</i>

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.060
My lord!

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:22.630
Hey.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:26.140
Who are you?

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:31.120
M-Me? I'm... Um, well, Hideyoshino...

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.730
I mean... I... I'm...!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:39.980
Um... People call me Hideyoshi.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.610
Hideyoshi?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.770
A good name.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.240
Who doesn't have a flush toilet by now?

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:11.770
Anyway, I followed them 
like they asked, but...

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.770
It's dark.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.830
What is this place?

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.340
Why don't they use any electricity?

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.760
Are they trying to save energy?

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.340
It gives the place atmosphere,

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:24.850
but the candles will strain my eyes.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.990
This mansion is huge, but...

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:31.810
I'm terribly sorry about this.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.530
It isn't your fault.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:34.710
Don't worry about it.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.270
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:39.580
<i>One girl looks just like Akerin.</i>

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:43.050
<i>And she and the other woman 
are both kinda weird.</i>

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.370
<i>I get it!</i>

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:45.800
<i>They're cosplayers!</i>

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.870
<i>And really into it!</i>

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.410
<i>That's gotta be it.</i>

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.120
<i>It's amazing how they've even done up</i>

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:52.540
<i>their house like this.</i>

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.680
<i>But where are we?</i>

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:58.360
Um... I should look at a map.

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:05.230
What is that?

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:08.150
It's a cell phone, of course!

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:10.570
This is the latest model!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:13.080
I'm going to use the GPS to find out...

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:16.190
It says out of range.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.460
Out of range?

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.550
The signal, you see...

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:21.510
The signal?

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.300
What are you talking about?

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:28.510
Um, well... I can't get a signal.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.400
What is this signal?

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.290
See?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:35.640
It's out of range, 
so I can't get even a single bar.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.560
B-Bar?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.770
See? It's out of range.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.770
<b>Out of Range</b>

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:43.520
Don't you find the reception's 
really bad here?

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:44.910
Give me that!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.720
This is what we do with things like this!

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.280
What are you doing?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.980
If a cuckoo won't sing, kill it.

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:58.010
If it's of no use, we simply destroy it!

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.720
You'll break it!

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.800
We just have to move to 
somewhere we can get reception!

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.470
How dare you speak to my lord that way?!

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:11.780
Hold a moment.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.010
Is it that important?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:19.270
Of course it is... I can't live without it.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.610
I see.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.640
It's not getting any reception...

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.570
Come on! Come on!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.660
Hey, listen to me!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:32.570
Hey, you.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.210
Will that cell phone of yours do much good?

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:39.810
Looks like it won't.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:41.830
I'm not getting any bars.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:45.050
My lord... This has gone far enough.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:47.700
We should get her out 
of the castle immediately...

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:47.700
Mitsuhide.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:50.840
I was thinking of having her help us.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.960
My lord! Do you feel quite well?

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:54.680
Indeed.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:58.480
We don't even know who she is!

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.490
Even for you, my lord, this isn't funny—

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:01.560
Mitsuhide.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:05.400
You must try to stop thinking with this,

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.820
and feel with this once in a while.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:15.360
She has a strange appearance,

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:17.160
but I think we can use her.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.660
Seriously? Her?

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.040
There is no reason.

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:25.290
My heart just feels this way.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:30.360
Um... You guys look like you've 
been discussing something,

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.280
without actually involving me—

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:33.470
What?

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.140
I want to go home...

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.200
Do you?

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:41.800
Very well.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.030
Was there always a big castle 
like this in my neighborhood?

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.500
Calm down.

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.240
Calm down, self!

00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:00.350
I remember going to a shrine, 
on the way back from school...

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.540
And then I bought a good-luck strap.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:06.150
And then there was this light, 
and the bell fell down.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.040
And then I woke up here...

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.760
Give her some money to get home.

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.130
This is money?

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:18.500
And...

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.540
Oda Nobunaga.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.900
A Warring States period general.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:28.980
Lived from 1534 to 1582...

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.660
I am Oda Nobunaga.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.950
My name is Akechi Mitsuhide.

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:39.460
E-Eiroku?

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.200
It's not the Heisei period?

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.100
Heisei?

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.660
What's that?

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:47.790
But why are they girls?

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:51.430
Something's weird...

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:00.120
It's all dark.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:01.730
Where's the station, anyway?

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:03.680
How do I get home?

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.780
It's so big...

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.930
I'm hungry.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.340
I want a hamburger.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.690
I can stop the diet for today, right?

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:18.580
Order a large fries...

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.910
There's no convenience store or anything?

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.010
Where am I, really?

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.170
Did I really...

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.190
No way, right?

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.140
What's wrong?

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.560
Weren't you going home?

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.550
I was going to,

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:55.760
but I can't find the station.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.640
And I don't even know 
what lines run through here.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:01.570
I don't think I can get home.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:04.520
What are you doing here?

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:08.230
W-Well... Ah, I was wondering 
if you had made it home.

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.170
Are you hungry?

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:16.760
No...

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.300
What's wrong?

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.140
Weren't you hungry?

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:29.120
It's not that. Do you have 
any ketchup or mayo?

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:30.230
Did you say something?

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:31.770
No...

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.270
By the way, you!

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.820
I'm told you will be relying 
upon our lord's beneficence.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:40.080
Um, you see, I don't know how to get home,

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.210
so I guess I'll be staying over—

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.800
But you'll be living here for a while, right?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:46.830
Y-Yes, unfortunately...

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.040
Then while you're here, 
make yourself useful to the lord.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.330
Would you help me?

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.740
I wish to conquer the land.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:58.260
Conquer?

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.490
What should I do?

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:04.800
Help me find the armor.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:15.360
For generations, this helmet has been 
passed down through the Oda family.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:20.100
I'd thought it a mere helmet 
and so I kept it in the storehouse,

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:23.590
but recently, I received a 
scroll that described

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.320
the "Crimson Armor."

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.330
This is what it said:

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.100
The general who wears this Crimson Armor

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:34.540
will certainly conquer the land.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.750
The legend says that the general

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.290
who wore this Crimson Armor

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:41.350
incurred the gods' wrath, and he lost his life.

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.760
And the armor was scattered and lost.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.470
When I heard this legend, I thought to myself,

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:51.300
were I to find all the armor's pieces,

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:55.690
it would hasten my long-cherished 
desire of conquest,

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:59.690
and I could unite the 
Land of the Rising Sun into one nation.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.340
<i>That was really complicated,</i>

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.100
<i>and I didn't get it all.</i>

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:10.820
<i>But basically, she wants to 
complete a set, right?</i>

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:11.870
<i>I guess.</i>

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.130
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:16.060
<i>I sometimes buy stuff,</i>

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.890
<i>just for the whole set bonus.</i>

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.340
OK, I'll help you!

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.090
She's taking this so easily.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:25.660
Will you?

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:26.840
I'm counting on you.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.170
Yes!

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:37.600
Well, I guess I can help out, 
until I find a way back home.

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:41.610
That Nobunaga seems like 
a pretty nice woman.

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:45.860
I have a lot of problems with this,

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:49.370
but I guess I can think about it tomorrow.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:53.160
Can't someone do something 
about this toilet?

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.170
A dog?

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:01.670
So cute!

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:03.430
It's got a helmet.

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:04.720
That's kinda silly!

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:07.380
Who the hell are you?

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:44.500
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:44.500
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:52.410
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:44.130
We'll practice the preview now!

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:46.100
Sounds boring!

00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:47.810
You say that, but you actually want to do it!

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.600
Would you stop being so optimistic?

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:52.410
Let's get started!

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.650
Preview

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.650
A Confused Maiden

00:23:52.650 --> 00:23:54.660
Look forward to next time!
